  "section_notes": "The final rules keep 55°C testing and a 5% corrective-action trigger but do not automatically ban sales above 5%, and per-model results go to customers and regulators but not the public. Remote shut-off retrofit is set at 6 years with a feasibility escape and local shut-off alternative; built-in suppression begins at 36 months. S5 retains a mandatory 8/100k recall with no transition and no corrective-action waiver, while S1 is limited to serious incidents and omits other-incident reporting."
